    <fr:title text="(TOP-X): rigidity of maximal modality">(TOP-X): rigidity of maximal modality</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>conjecture</fr:taxon>
    <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="area">frontier</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="status">open</fr:meta>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>(TOP-X). Every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[U]]></fr:tex>-stable irreducible <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[W]]></fr:tex> with maximal
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\operatorname {umod}(W)]]></fr:tex> is dense in a maximizer sweep stratum.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Role in the skeleton.</html:strong> This is what carries <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0040/" title="The M-law: the unimodal side of the leading-term law" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0040/" display-uri="ffi-0040" type="local">the M-law</fr:link> across to <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\operatorname {lc} \kappa (U_{n})]]></fr:tex>:
without it, the argmax count over parabolic nilradicals need not be the
count of top-dimensional sweep strata, and
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0039/" title="The leading-term law" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0039/" display-uri="ffi-0039" type="local">the leading-term law</fr:link> does not follow. It is the
leading-coefficient twin of the rigidity statements the height ladder
needs.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> Proven for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  16]]></fr:tex> by Corollary F's squeeze — which is also
why the leading-term law is verified exactly on the range where
published values exist. Open in general.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0028/" title="U-modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0028/" display-uri="ffi-0028" type="local">U-modality</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0034/" title="(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0034/" display-uri="ffi-0034" type="local">(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions</fr:link>.</html:p>
    <html:p>
      <html:em>Provenance: scratch_nineteenth.md route (a); Corollary F.</html:em>
    </html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
